  "comments": "<p>Four main types are known.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - large details, legend ends at the bottom to the left of a pearl.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - smaller details, legend ends at the bottom under a pearl.<br><br><i>Reverse</i><br>Die <strong>A</strong> - wide vertical stripes, vivid script of denomination in Arabic.<br>Die <strong>B</strong> - narrow vertical stripes, fine fonts, canonical script of denomination in Arabic.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61bf28305aff8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61bf28305aff8.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><i>Note</i>. There are much more differences between dies, these were marked for easy attribution.<br><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>1</strong>+<strong>A</strong>: 5755, 5758, 5762, 5765↑↑, 5765↑↓, 5766, 5769.<br><strong>1</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: 5770.<br><strong>2</strong>+<strong>A</strong>: 5766.<br><strong>2</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: <strong><u>5770</u></strong>-5777.</p>",
